(1309866, 165989, 2170, '<td valign="top">good picture -- and he''s got a rockin'' name, too.  i like the vignetting.</td>', 'good picture -- and he''s got a rockin'' name, too.  i like the vignetting.', '2005-04-21 00:42:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309867, 167816, 2170, '<td valign="top">great capture.  i wish it were not blurry.</td>', 'great capture.  i wish it were not blurry.', '2005-04-21 00:43:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309869, 167667, 2170, '<td valign="top">i love offbeat shots like this.  great job.</td>', 'i love offbeat shots like this.  great job.', '2005-04-21 00:44:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309872, 167616, 2170, '<td valign="top">great capture.  really tells a story.</td>', 'great capture.  really tells a story.', '2005-04-21 00:46:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309875, 167194, 2170, '<td valign="top">i love the really strong contrast here.</td>', 'i love the really strong contrast here.', '2005-04-21 00:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309903, 167706, 10261, '<td valign="top">This would be much more powerful if I could see the model''s face a little better. The contrast is good, but the expression would be more apparent if the light side were lighter. Moving the light source to a position less behind the model might help.</td>', 'This would be much more powerful if I could see the model''s face a little better. The contrast is good, but the expression would be more apparent if the light side were lighter. Moving the light source to a position less behind the model might help.', '2005-04-21 00:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309907, 167459, 10261, '<td valign="top">The hue is a bit too green for my tastes, and I''m not sure that I like the missing chin/ear. Good repetition of textures between his facial hair and the wall.<br/></td>', 'The hue is a bit too green for my tastes, and I''m not sure that I like the missing chin/ear. Good repetition of textures between his facial hair and the wall.', '2005-04-21 00:58:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309915, 167539, 10261, '<td valign="top">The effect really shows off the kid''s eyes. Unfortunately he looks like he''s about to fall asleep. Because of this the result seems closer to "undead zombie child" than "blue eyes win blue ribbons".</td>', 'The effect really shows off the kid''s eyes. Unfortunately he looks like he''s about to fall asleep. Because of this the result seems closer to "undead zombie child" than "blue eyes win blue ribbons".', '2005-04-21 01:03:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309920, 167793, 10261, '<td valign="top">She looks rather stiff and uncomfortable, giving this picture an overly-staged feel.</td>', 'She looks rather stiff and uncomfortable, giving this picture an overly-staged feel.', '2005-04-21 01:04:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309923, 165314, 10261, '<td valign="top">The hood of the car is distracting. Since the officer''s legs don''t seem to add much to this shot you might have been better off cropping them off at the knees.<br/></td>', 'The hood of the car is distracting. Since the officer''s legs don''t seem to add much to this shot you might have been better off cropping them off at the knees.', '2005-04-21 01:05:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309937, 167414, 10261, '<td valign="top">Good use of bokeh, but the contrasty blobs in the background do still detract somewhat from the image.<br/></td>', 'Good use of bokeh, but the contrasty blobs in the background do still detract somewhat from the image.', '2005-04-21 01:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309957, 167671, 10261, '<td valign="top">This just screams "snapshot". The unkempt appearance of the kid makes this a sub-par photograph, even by snapshot standards.<br/> <br/>At DPC, pictures of kids tend to be graded by a slightly different standard than some other subjects. So unless the image is well done (from a photographic, compositional standpoint) they usually don''t score well. When the parent sees a picture like this they may feel a rush of love and adoration. But since the rest of us have no such attachment to the kid, all we see is what''s in the picture. In this case the picture contains a messy looking baby.<br/></td>', 'This just screams "snapshot". The unkempt appearance of the kid makes this a sub-par photograph, even by snapshot standards. At DPC, pictures of kids tend to be graded by a slightly different standard than some other subjects. So unless the image is well done (from a photographic, compositional standpoint) they usually don''t score well. When the parent sees a picture like this they may feel a rush of love and adoration. But since the rest of us have no such attachment to the kid, all we see is what''s in the picture. In this case the picture contains a messy looking baby.', '2005-04-21 01:20:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309963, 167735, 10261, '<td valign="top">Even aside from making the subjects squint, the harsh lighting here works against capturing a good image here. You might have been able to salvage this by placing a reflector on the ground in front of the kids, but the real solution is to avoid shooting in direct sunlight.</td>', 'Even aside from making the subjects squint, the harsh lighting here works against capturing a good image here. You might have been able to salvage this by placing a reflector on the ground in front of the kids, but the real solution is to avoid shooting in direct sunlight.', '2005-04-21 01:23:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309975, 167594, 10261, '<td valign="top">Was this shot using a fisheye lens? This image looks distorted, almost as though the model''s head is too big for her body. The soft focus works well here, but the distortion makes this look less like a portrait and more like a bobble-head figurine.</td>', 'Was this shot using a fisheye lens? This image looks distorted, almost as though the model''s head is too big for her body. The soft focus works well here, but the distortion makes this look less like a portrait and more like a bobble-head figurine.', '2005-04-21 01:27:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309979, 167790, 10261, '<td valign="top">The angular crop looks more like a creative attempt to rescue a photograph than a stylistic decision made when shooting. The disembodied beer drinking arm on the left is distracting. <br/></td>', 'The angular crop looks more like a creative attempt to rescue a photograph than a stylistic decision made when shooting. The disembodied beer drinking arm on the left is distracting. ', '2005-04-21 01:29:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309980, 167610, 9809, '<td valign="top">Eyes, scarf, excellent. Eyes -- incredible. The white space on the left I''m not liking so much. I would have preferred it cropped more on the left with possible white space on the right -- the direction she is looking, sort of.</td>', 'Eyes, scarf, excellent. Eyes -- incredible. The white space on the left I''m not liking so much. I would have preferred it cropped more on the left with possible white space on the right -- the direction she is looking, sort of.', '2005-04-21 01:30:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309986, 167686, 10261, '<td valign="top">If I didn''t know better, I''d think that Anthony was trying to wish me away into the corn field.<br/> <br/>Good DOF. I''m not sure that I like the arms reaching out of the frame, but it does seem to hint at a reason for his penetrating stare. Although I''m not typically a fan of selective desaturation, desaturating everything but his eyes might have given this image that extra kick needed to score within the top 30%.</td>', 'If I didn''t know better, I''d think that Anthony was trying to wish me away into the corn field. Good DOF. I''m not sure that I like the arms reaching out of the frame, but it does seem to hint at a reason for his penetrating stare. Although I''m not typically a fan of selective desaturation, desaturating everything but his eyes might have given this image that extra kick needed to score within the top 30%.', '2005-04-21 01:34:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309988, 167670, 9809, '<td valign="top">Just a touch dark. A little softer focus on the background would be nice, but what you have is OK. Perfect catch on expression. Nice job of cropping/framing.</td>', 'Just a touch dark. A little softer focus on the background would be nice, but what you have is OK. Perfect catch on expression. Nice job of cropping/framing.', '2005-04-21 01:34:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309996, 167746, 10261, '<td valign="top">"Well let''s see here. I remember takin'' something out of the glass on the dresser and puttin'' it in my mouth this mornin'', but I also had to gum my way through the runny eggs at breakfast. I sure hope that I didn''t just swallow another goldfish..."<br/> <br/>This guy''s face hints at an interesting personality. I can''t help but think that you could have caught him at a more flattering moment though.</td>', '"Well let''s see here. I remember takin'' something out of the glass on the dresser and puttin'' it in my mouth this mornin'', but I also had to gum my way through the runny eggs at breakfast. I sure hope that I didn''t just swallow another goldfish..." This guy''s face hints at an interesting personality. I can''t help but think that you could have caught him at a more flattering moment though.', '2005-04-21 01:39:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1309998, 167143, 10261, '<td valign="top">This picture looks a touch grainy, but otherwise a very solid entry.</td>', 'This picture looks a touch grainy, but otherwise a very solid entry.', '2005-04-21 01:40:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310001, 167193, 675, '<td valign="top">this is one of the funniest photos i''ve seen in a long time</td>', 'this is one of the funniest photos i''ve seen in a long time', '2005-04-21 01:41:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310002, 167256, 10261, '<td valign="top">Due to the unfortunate angle the outlooks seem to be from inside the carriage and from inside the horse''s hindquarters. Since the rest of the image looks static, the lone blurry hoof stands out a bit too much.<br/></td>', 'Due to the unfortunate angle the outlooks seem to be from inside the carriage and from inside the horse''s hindquarters. Since the rest of the image looks static, the lone blurry hoof stands out a bit too much.', '2005-04-21 01:42:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310004, 167650, 10261, '<td valign="top">The background is cluttered and the foreground doesn''t hold much interest.</td>', 'The background is cluttered and the foreground doesn''t hold much interest.', '2005-04-21 01:44:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310011, 167204, 10261, '<td valign="top">If the challenge topic was "open spaces" or something similar I''d give this high marks. As it is the people-like things are little more than black specks.</td>', 'If the challenge topic was "open spaces" or something similar I''d give this high marks. As it is the people-like things are little more than black specks.', '2005-04-21 01:48:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310015, 167704, 10261, '<td valign="top">The strong shadow under his chin bothers me, as does the odd glow where the image meets the border.</td>', 'The strong shadow under his chin bothers me, as does the odd glow where the image meets the border.', '2005-04-21 01:49:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310018, 167425, 10261, '<td valign="top">This is one of those cases where a little more motion blur would have helped your score. I think that I may have preferred to see this with the background only partially desaturated.</td>', 'This is one of those cases where a little more motion blur would have helped your score. I think that I may have preferred to see this with the background only partially desaturated.', '2005-04-21 01:50:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310024, 166782, 10261, '<td valign="top">This feels more like a "I bumped the shutter button while stepping off of the bus" shot than a premeditated candid. The B&amp;W does add a somewhat more refined air to the picture  though.</td>', 'This feels more like a "I bumped the shutter button while stepping off of the bus" shot than a premeditated candid. The B&W does add a somewhat more refined air to the picture  though.', '2005-04-21 01:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310031, 167809, 10261, '<td valign="top">The contrast seems a little low &amp;/or the shot is slightly underexposed. A catchlight would have really helped to emphasize his eyes. As it is I can''t see any clear boundary between his iris and pupil.</td>', 'The contrast seems a little low &/or the shot is slightly underexposed. A catchlight would have really helped to emphasize his eyes. As it is I can''t see any clear boundary between his iris and pupil.', '2005-04-21 01:55:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310038, 167811, 10261, '<td valign="top">The harsh highlights combined with the murky shadows seriously detract from the image. The highlight on the guy''s hand / chin is quite distracting. Since the couple seems to be the focus of the image the DOF should have been shallow enough to render the guy with the shiny glasses as a shadowy blob. The clutter on the left side of the image seems to serve no purpose. Even if all these technical issues were fixed I''m still not convinced I''d find the couple particularly interesting.</td>', 'The harsh highlights combined with the murky shadows seriously detract from the image. The highlight on the guy''s hand / chin is quite distracting. Since the couple seems to be the focus of the image the DOF should have been shallow enough to render the guy with the shiny glasses as a shadowy blob. The clutter on the left side of the image seems to serve no purpose. Even if all these technical issues were fixed I''m still not convinced I''d find the couple particularly interesting.', '2005-04-21 02:00:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1310046, 167825, 10261, '<td valign="top">I''d give the guy a few bucks just for the chance to ask him whether his honesty got him more money than a more typical "help a Vietnam vet" type sign.<br/> <br/>I think that the blurry cars in the background, while a bit more distracting than I''d like, do help to emphasize his separation from the rest of the city dwellers.</td>', 'I''d give the guy a few bucks just for the chance to ask him whether his honesty got him more money than a more typical "help a Vietnam vet" type sign. I think that the blurry cars in the background, while a bit more distracting than I''d like, do help to emphasize his separation from the rest of the city dwellers.', '2005-04-21 02:05:35.000000', NULL, 1),
