(1313987, 167259, 31213, '<td valign="top">I know you went for something edgy but I think you tried a little too hard to "get outside the box".  Goodluck!</td>', 'I know you went for something edgy but I think you tried a little too hard to "get outside the box".  Goodluck!', '2005-04-22 18:35:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314001, 167079, 31213, '<td valign="top">Your subject kind of gets lost in the picture.  Well composed though and I love the ladder reflection in the mirror, adds semetry to the shot.</td>', 'Your subject kind of gets lost in the picture.  Well composed though and I love the ladder reflection in the mirror, adds semetry to the shot.', '2005-04-22 18:42:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314003, 167078, 31213, '<td valign="top">This shot has a desperate need for a backlight.  This would bring your subject out of the shadows and help seperate her from the background.  Its okay....next time!  :)</td>', 'This shot has a desperate need for a backlight.  This would bring your subject out of the shadows and help seperate her from the background.  Its okay....next time!  :)', '2005-04-22 18:43:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314008, 167583, 31213, '<td valign="top">LOL.  Saw the pic and thought, "cool".  Then I read the title and really got a chuckle.  It gave the photograph a lighter tone and made it comical.  Lots of distracting people and elements in this shot....the stroller is blocking part of your subject!  BUT, I understand this was a true candid shot and so I can''t be too harsh.  Nice capture.<br/> <br/>Happy Shooting!<br/> <br/>Chris A</td>', 'LOL.  Saw the pic and thought, "cool".  Then I read the title and really got a chuckle.  It gave the photograph a lighter tone and made it comical.  Lots of distracting people and elements in this shot....the stroller is blocking part of your subject!  BUT, I understand this was a true candid shot and so I can''t be too harsh.  Nice capture. Happy Shooting! Chris A', '2005-04-22 18:46:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314010, 167834, 31213, '<td valign="top">Looks like quite a party!  Very well lit.  The high key lighting really works here to help punch the dark skin and keep is contrasty to the background.</td>', 'Looks like quite a party!  Very well lit.  The high key lighting really works here to help punch the dark skin and keep is contrasty to the background.', '2005-04-22 18:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314012, 167591, 31213, '<td valign="top">Without the person, this could be a postcard!  Some interesting post processing on this one....but I think it works well with the emotion of the photo.  Very nice.</td>', 'Without the person, this could be a postcard!  Some interesting post processing on this one....but I think it works well with the emotion of the photo.  Very nice.', '2005-04-22 18:47:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314014, 167125, 31213, '<td valign="top">Its all about the angles!  Nice work.  One of a kind in this challenge.</td>', 'Its all about the angles!  Nice work.  One of a kind in this challenge.', '2005-04-22 18:48:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314016, 167080, 31213, '<td valign="top">Great dark blacks.  I feel like I''m there when I look at this picture.  Keep up the great work!<br/> <br/>Happy shooting,<br/>Chris A</td>', 'Great dark blacks.  I feel like I''m there when I look at this picture.  Keep up the great work! Happy shooting,Chris A', '2005-04-22 18:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314023, 167154, 31213, '<td valign="top">Selective desat is scary, but this isn''t too extreme and kind of works.  Nice job.  When I look at this picture, I can hear him playing.</td>', 'Selective desat is scary, but this isn''t too extreme and kind of works.  Nice job.  When I look at this picture, I can hear him playing.', '2005-04-22 18:51:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314038, 167360, 31213, '<td valign="top">This probably is getting about a 5.1 and you''re probably wondering why.  I could be wrong....I''m just giving it a go though.<br/> <br/>I think it feels snapshotty.  It looks like while on the hike you just whipped out the cam and, without putting too much thought into it, you snapped the shot, then kept walking.  I mean, don''t get me wrong, it looks like a pretty area, but to sell the hardass voters, you''re going to have to get a little more unique and thoughtfull.<br/> <br/>The angle is normal eye height, your subject is dead center of the image (no rule of thirds or strong compositional lines), the lighting is blown out in the background and still a bit dark in the foreground.<br/> <br/>I''m not trying to just rip into you, but I figure this pic will get lost in the lower half of the challenge and people often dont spend the time to really critique images they rate.  I get so frustrated when I get a low score, and no good feedback.  <br/> <br/>You may completely disagree with everything I said, but thats just my 2 cents, so take it with a grain of salt.  I hope your pic does great and proves me wrong!<br/> <br/>Happy shooting,<br/> <br/>Chris A</td>', 'This probably is getting about a 5.1 and you''re probably wondering why.  I could be wrong....I''m just giving it a go though. I think it feels snapshotty.  It looks like while on the hike you just whipped out the cam and, without putting too much thought into it, you snapped the shot, then kept walking.  I mean, don''t get me wrong, it looks like a pretty area, but to sell the hardass voters, you''re going to have to get a little more unique and thoughtfull. The angle is normal eye height, your subject is dead center of the image (no rule of thirds or strong compositional lines), the lighting is blown out in the background and still a bit dark in the foreground. I''m not trying to just rip into you, but I figure this pic will get lost in the lower half of the challenge and people often dont spend the time to really critique images they rate.  I get so frustrated when I get a low score, and no good feedback.   You may completely disagree with everything I said, but thats just my 2 cents, so take it with a grain of salt.  I hope your pic does great and proves me wrong! Happy shooting, Chris A', '2005-04-22 19:04:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1314069, 166160, 5286, '<td valign="top">There''s a lot of potential in this picture, but I think it needs some more work to bring it out. The subjects are very sweet, and you have captured a great moment. A couple of things though. The girl''s face is cutoff at the ear, and that is very distracting. Also the focus is not sharp enough, the light is bland. A little work in PS with curves, and some dodging of the eyes can help with this.  Also with the composition as it is, the eye flits back and forth between the children and finally settles on the background, which incidentally seems to be pretty well focused. <br/>You have photogenic subjects, though, esp. the little girl. You could probably get a stunning shot of just her with some good light and sharp focusing on the eyes. <br/></td>', 'There''s a lot of potential in this picture, but I think it needs some more work to bring it out. The subjects are very sweet, and you have captured a great moment. A couple of things though. The girl''s face is cutoff at the ear, and that is very distracting. Also the focus is not sharp enough, the light is bland. A little work in PS with curves, and some dodging of the eyes can help with this.  Also with the composition as it is, the eye flits back and forth between the children and finally settles on the background, which incidentally seems to be pretty well focused. You have photogenic subjects, though, esp. the little girl. You could probably get a stunning shot of just her with some good light and sharp focusing on the eyes. ', '2005-04-22 19:30:06.000000', NULL, 1),
