(1333324, 167437, 5286, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on another ribbon! I was totally fooled by Philos31''s image which I thought was yours... and when I voted on this I said to myself someone else is using Librodo''s kind of light :D... lovely image. I particularly like how the net in the background adds to the picture, in another composition it might have been just an irritating background object but here it adds a lot to the picture. And an excellent light, as always!</td>', 'Congratulations on another ribbon! I was totally fooled by Philos31''s image which I thought was yours... and when I voted on this I said to myself someone else is using Librodo''s kind of light :D... lovely image. I particularly like how the net in the background adds to the picture, in another composition it might have been just an irritating background object but here it adds a lot to the picture. And an excellent light, as always!', '2005-04-27 14:08:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1333839, 167143, 5286, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the blue with an excellent image! I wanted this one to ribbon so much, I''m glad it did :) Good work, and keep them coming!</td>', 'Congratulations on the blue with an excellent image! I wanted this one to ribbon so much, I''m glad it did :) Good work, and keep them coming!', '2005-04-27 15:49:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1334067, 167531, 34664, '<td valign="top">In retrospect I wished I had cropped out more of the red carpet start line. My pics from after the race started were not as interesting.</td>', 'In retrospect I wished I had cropped out more of the red carpet start line. My pics from after the race started were not as interesting.', '2005-04-27 16:46:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1335675, 166548, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>OK, first thing that stands out as a negative here is the corner of the TV.  There''s a little section of background that is a slight lighter color than the TV and it''s in the upper left.  With you being in the lower left, I think that it''s a bit of a distraction from you.<br/>Focus and clarity look great, especially for being a low light shot.<br/>I love the framing/cropping you chose.  I think the negative space works really well in a shot such as this.<br/>Side note...I really REALLY want a Snickers candybar right now.<br/>The lighting in my opinion is great.  I like how it hides features and shows others.  This photo shows that you can still be a ''tough guy'' and still ''pose'' for photos.<br/>I personally think this should have scored higher, but I''m a little odd like that anyway.  Nice one.<br/>~Heather~<br/></td>', '*Critique Club* OK, first thing that stands out as a negative here is the corner of the TV.  There''s a little section of background that is a slight lighter color than the TV and it''s in the upper left.  With you being in the lower left, I think that it''s a bit of a distraction from you.Focus and clarity look great, especially for being a low light shot.I love the framing/cropping you chose.  I think the negative space works really well in a shot such as this.Side note...I really REALLY want a Snickers candybar right now.The lighting in my opinion is great.  I like how it hides features and shows others.  This photo shows that you can still be a ''tough guy'' and still ''pose'' for photos.I personally think this should have scored higher, but I''m a little odd like that anyway.  Nice one.~Heather~', '2005-04-27 23:26:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1335925, 167143, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Wow...what can I say that 120+ people didn''t already say?<br/>The first thing I notice about it is that it seems very speckled.  Oversharpened?  I love the shot and it is very detailed and visually appealing.<br/>Great focus and lighting.  The left (her right) gets a tad bright, but it does not distract from the photo at all.  Actually, it could even be a plus.<br/>The hair in the face is a little strong, but not distracting.  The eyes are captivating.<br/>Not really much that I can add...simply wonderful.  ~Heather~</td>', '*Critique Club* Wow...what can I say that 120+ people didn''t already say?The first thing I notice about it is that it seems very speckled.  Oversharpened?  I love the shot and it is very detailed and visually appealing.Great focus and lighting.  The left (her right) gets a tad bright, but it does not distract from the photo at all.  Actually, it could even be a plus.The hair in the face is a little strong, but not distracting.  The eyes are captivating.Not really much that I can add...simply wonderful.  ~Heather~', '2005-04-28 00:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
